### 4.3 Download the SCOS Image

Create a directory for the OS image:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/okd-images
cd ~/okd-images
```

Download the exact SCOS image selected in Section 4.2:

```bash
curl -LO <SCOS-IMAGE-URL>
```

For this lab, the selected image was:

```text
scos-10.0.20251103-0-openstack.x86_64
```

Verify that the image was downloaded:

```bash
ls -lh
```

Check the image format:

```bash
file scos-10.0.20251103-0-openstack.x86_64
```

For additional verification:

```bash
qemu-img info scos-10.0.20251103-0-openstack.x86_64
```

Confirm:

```text
file format: qcow2
```

### Checksum Verification

Calculate the SHA-256 checksum:

```bash
sha256sum scos-10.0.20251103-0-openstack.x86_64
```

Compare the result with the checksum published for the **exact same image**.

The checksum must match before proceeding.

### Verification Checklist

```text
[ ] Image downloaded
[ ] Correct image filename
[ ] Architecture is x86_64
[ ] Image format is QCOW2
[ ] SHA-256 checksum matches
```

The verified image is now ready to be uploaded to OCI Object Storage.